AI Overview
AI

!!!Introduction

The <*AI*> library (<*PocoAI*>, namespace <[Poco::AI]>) runs agents on large language
models: providers for the Anthropic Messages API and for the OpenAI Chat Completions API and
the servers compatible with it, a registry of tools, an agent loop that calls the model and
runs the tools it asks for, and a host that gives the model the tools of MCP servers.

The library is experimental: its API may change within POCO 2.x.

Dependencies: Foundation, JSON, Net, AI/MCP and AI/MCP/HTTP; NetSSL for https endpoints.


!!!Classes

<[LLMProvider]> is the interface of a model API. <[LLMProvider::chat()]> makes one call: it
delivers the text as it streams in, as <[ContentEvent]>s, and returns a <[ChatResult]> with
the stop reason, the usage, the tool calls and the model's turn in the provider's own message
format, which the caller appends to the conversation unchanged.
<[LLMProvider::appendToolResult()]> adds a tool result in that format.

<[AnthropicProvider]> and <[OpenAIProvider]> are the two providers. Each takes its settings in
a <*Params*> structure: the base URI, the API key, the model, the token limit, the timeout,
members to merge into every request body, and headers to send with every request. Sessions
come from a session factory, so that an application can use a proxy, its own TLS context or a
tunnel.

<[Cancellation]> is the token of one call or one run, which another thread may cancel. A
cancel ends a call in any phase, connecting, sending, or reading the stream, by shutting its
connection down. Calls that share a provider each have their own token.

<[ToolRegistry]> holds the tools an agent may call, as <[Poco::AI::MCP::Tool]> definitions
with handlers that return a <[Poco::AI::MCP::ToolResult]>: the same tool model as an MCP
server's.

<[AgentLoop]> runs an agent: it calls the model, runs the tools it calls, passes the results
back, and repeats until the model answers without tool calls, the run is cancelled, a call
fails, the token limit cuts an answer, or the round limit is reached. It reports every step as
an <[AgentEvent]> and ends every run with a DONE event that carries the stop reason of the
last call and the usage of all. Every tool call in the conversation gets its result, so the
conversation stays one the model APIs accept. An approver decides which calls run.

<[MCPHost]> connects to MCP servers over any <[Poco::AI::MCP::Client]>, stdio or Streamable
HTTP, and registers their tools in a <[ToolRegistry]>.


!!!Security

Tool results, the descriptions of tools from remote servers and the input a model gives a tool
are untrusted input. A model may call a tool with arguments it chose after reading text an
attacker wrote. Let a person or a policy decide, with an approver
(<[AgentLoop::setApprover()]>), which calls run.


!!!Building AI

!!CMake

The CMake option <*ENABLE_AI*> is off by default; it turns on <*ENABLE_AI_MCP*> and
<*ENABLE_AI_MCP_HTTP*>.

    cmake -B build -DENABLE_AI=ON
    cmake --build build

!!GNU Make

The component <*AI*> is omitted from the typical configuration, together with <*AI/MCP*> and
<*AI/MCP/HTTP*>. Configure with <*--everything*>, or with an <*--omit*> list that does not
name <*AI*>.


!!!Example

The following program gives a model served by a local ollama one tool and asks it a question.
For an https endpoint, such as the Anthropic or the OpenAI API, register
<[Poco::Net::HTTPSSessionInstantiator]> first, or give the provider a session factory.

    #include "Poco/AI/AgentLoop.h"
    #include "Poco/AI/OpenAIProvider.h"
    #include "Poco/AI/ToolRegistry.h"
    #include "Poco/DateTimeFormat.h"
    #include "Poco/DateTimeFormatter.h"
    #include "Poco/Timestamp.h"
    #include <iostream>
    #include <memory>

    using namespace Poco::AI;

    int main()
    {
        OpenAIProvider::Params params;
        params.baseURI = Poco::URI("http://localhost:11434/v1");
        params.model = "qwen3";
        auto pProvider = std::make_shared<OpenAIProvider>(params);

        ToolRegistry tools;
        tools.registerTool("time", "Returns the current time, in UTC.", nullptr,
            [](const Poco::JSON::Object::Ptr&)
            {
                return Poco::DateTimeFormatter::format(Poco::Timestamp(), Poco::DateTimeFormat::ISO8601_FORMAT);
            });

        AgentLoop loop(pProvider, tools);
        Poco::JSON::Array conversation;
        Poco::JSON::Object::Ptr pQuestion = new Poco::JSON::Object;
        pQuestion->set("role", "user");
        pQuestion->set("content", "What time is it in Tokyo?");
        conversation.add(pQuestion);

        loop.run(conversation, "Answer briefly.", [](const AgentEvent& event)
        {
            if (event.type == AgentEvent::Type::TEXT) std::cout << event.content << std::flush;
            if (event.type == AgentEvent::Type::FAILURE) std::cerr << event.content << std::endl;
        });
        std::cout << std::endl;
        return 0;
    }
